            <ArticleTitle>Recurrent infections and cows-milk hypersensitivity in a 2-year-old girl with hyper immunoglobulin E syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>299-303</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">010.04/ijaai.299303</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The hyperimmunoglobulin E syndrome is a rare complex primary immunodeficiency characterized by high serum IgE levels, eczema, and recurrent infections. We present a case of 2-years-old girl with eczema and repeated bacterial skin and lung infections since the period of infancy. The patient also had eosinophilia, high serum levels of IgE, and cows-milk hypersensitivity. We describe the case, in order to illustrate the difficulty of establishing the diagnosis hyper-immunoglobulin E syndrome in a toddler.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
